<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">James Brooke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1803–1868</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Rajah James Brooke</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">James Brooke was an English adventurer who helped the Brunei Sultanate put down a revolt near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kuching">Kuching</a> and in 1841 was made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajah-of-sarawak">Rajah of Sarawak</a>. He founded the dynasty of the White Rajahs, which ruled Sarawak for a century. He also served as the first governor of the crown colony of Labuan from 1848.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/james-brooke.jpg" alt="James Brooke" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Herbert Watkins · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sir-James-Brooke.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
